      "message": "Let\u0027s make these strongly-typed with `enum class`. Gemini instructions to implement this:\n\n---\n\nYou should move these into `enum class Command : uint8_t` and `enum class Status : uint8_t`.\n\n**Why?**\n\n* **Type Safety:** It makes it impossible to accidentally pass a status code where a command code is expected, or to perform meaningless math on them.\n* **Struct Integration:** Because you are using C++ and `__attribute__((packed))` structs, you can safely use these strongly-typed enums directly inside your `IapCommandPacket` and `IapStatusPacket`. This eliminates casting and makes the structs self-documenting.\n\n---\n\n### How to Implement the Change\n\nHere is how you can cleanly refactor the commands and status values.\n\n#### Step 1: Update the Packet Structs\n\nMove the definitions outside the class (or to the top of `iap_control.h`) so the packet structs can use them.\n\n**File:** `util/elan/iap_control.h`\n\n```cpp\nnamespace elan {\n\nenum class Command : uint8_t {\n  RunIap \u003d 0x20,\n  FinishedIap \u003d 0x21,\n  SoftwareReset \u003d 0x22,\n  GetFwVersion \u003d 0x41,\n  AbortProcess \u003d 0x48,\n  WriteRom \u003d 0xA0,\n  WriteRomFinish \u003d 0xA1,\n  SetRomAddress \u003d 0xA4,\n  ReadRom \u003d 0xE0,\n  ReadRomFinish \u003d 0xE1,\n};\n\nenum class Status : uint8_t {\n  Ready \u003d 0x00,\n  Success \u003d 0x01,\n};\n\n// Update the structs to use the strongly-typed enums!\nstruct IapCommandPacket {\n  Command cmd_code;        // \u003c-- Now strongly typed\n  uint8_t reserved;\n  uint8_t parameter_2[2];\n  union {\n    uint32_t payload_le;\n    uint8_t iap_mode;\n  };\n  // ... AsByteSpan() ...\n} __attribute__((packed));\n\nstruct IapStatusPacket {\n  Command cmd_echo;        // \u003c-- Now strongly typed\n  Status status_code;      // \u003c-- Now strongly typed\n  uint8_t parameter_2[2];\n  uint32_t parameter_1;\n  // ... AsByteSpan() ...\n} __attribute__((packed));\n\n```\n\n#### Step 2: Clean Up the Class Header\n\nRemove the old command/status `constexpr` definitions, but keep the endpoints and magic values.\n\n**File:** `util/elan/iap_control.h`\n\n```cpp\nclass IapControl {\n  // ...\n  // --- USB Endpoints \u0026 Lengths ---\n  static constexpr uint8_t kEpCmdOut \u003d 0x01;\n  static constexpr uint8_t kEpStatusIn \u003d 0x82;\n  static constexpr uint8_t kEpDataOut \u003d 0x03;\n  static constexpr uint8_t kEpDataIn \u003d 0x84;\n  static constexpr size_t kEpDataLength \u003d 64;\n\n  // --- Magic Values ---\n  static constexpr uint8_t kGoogleFwVerPrefix \u003d 0x10;\n  static constexpr uint32_t kBaseRomAddress \u003d 0x0000;\n\n private:\n  // Update signatures to expect the strong type\n  std::expected\u003cvoid, IapError\u003e SendCmdOnly(Command cmd_code);\n  std::expected\u003cvoid, IapError\u003e SendCmdWithU32Payload(Command cmd_code,\n                                                      uint32_t payload_val);\n  // ...\n};\n\n```\n\n#### Step 3: Update the Implementation\n\nUpdate your `iap_control.cc` to use the new scoped enum values.\n\n**File:** `util/elan/iap_control.cc`\n\n```cpp\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, IapError\u003e IapControl::RunIap(uint8_t iap_mode) {\n  // Designated initializers work beautifully here\n  IapCommandPacket packet \u003d {.cmd_code \u003d Command::RunIap,\n                             .reserved \u003d 0,\n                             .parameter_2 \u003d {0},\n                             .iap_mode \u003d iap_mode};\n  return IapCommand(packet);\n}\n\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, IapError\u003e IapControl::FinishIap(uint32_t checksum) {\n  return SendCmdWithU32Payload(Command::FinishedIap, checksum);\n}\n\n// ... update other calls similarly (e.g., Command::WriteRom)\n\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, IapError\u003e IapControl::IapCommand(\n    const IapCommandPacket \u0026packet) {\n  // ...\n  \n  // Checking status is now strongly typed and readable\n  if (stat_recv.cmd_echo !\u003d packet.cmd_code ||\n      stat_recv.status_code !\u003d Status: